DS3D glprocess is the OpenGL ES rendering back-end shared by the DS3D data
render modules. It wraps GLFW window management, GLES3 shader programs, vertex
and texture buffers, CUDA/GL interop, and pango/cairo text rasterization into
the render-context interfaces declared in `glprocess/gl_render_ctx.h` and
`glprocess/window.h`.

DS3D is framework agnostic. There is no gstreamer/Glib dependency for the
rendering itself; glib is pulled in only indirectly through pangocairo.

`libnvds_3d_glprocess.so` is built from these source files. It is not loaded as
a `ds3d::` custom module — it is linked directly by the data render libraries:

    libnvds_3d_gl_datarender.so           datarender/gl3d
    libnvds_3d_gles_ensemble_render.so    datarender/gl3d_ensemble

The render contexts it provides are:

    gl_depth_render_ctx.h        depth-image render context
    gl_point_cloud_render_ctx.h  coloured point-cloud render context
    gl_lidar_render_ctx.h        LiDAR point-cloud and bounding-box render context
    gl_texture_render.h          RGB texture render context
    gl_text.h                    pango/cairo text overlay

GLFW and GLM headers are taken from the system libglfw3-dev and libglm-dev
packages rather than being vendored in this tree.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://nvidia-deepstream.docs.buildwithfern.com/deepstream/9.2/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libglfw3 Development package
- libglm Development package
- libgles2 / libegl1 Development packages
- libpango1.0 and libcairo2 Development packages
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- libx11 Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvds_3d_glprocess.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
